# Cache policy for the asset store. Parsed by Workers, never served itself.
#
# Workers' default for every static asset is `public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate`, which is a safe default and the wrong one here in two ways.
#
# It made the hover prefetch useless. A response that must be revalidated
# cannot be reused from cache, so the document Astro had already fetched was
# thrown away and refetched on the click. Meanwhile the stylesheet -- also
# revalidated, but tiny and answered with a 304 -- was ready first, so the
# browser had enough to paint a styled header over bare background while the
# body was still arriving. That frame is the flash of black between pages.
#
# It also revalidates fingerprinted files on every navigation. Those URLs
# change whenever their content does, so the round trip can never do anything
# except confirm what the URL already promised.

# Everything, unless overridden below. A minute of freshness is what makes a
# prefetched page reusable on the click; `must-revalidate` then forbids serving
# it stale, so a deploy is picked up a minute later at the outside.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, must-revalidate

# Astro fingerprints everything it emits here, so these are safe to keep for a
# year and never revalidate. The detach is deliberate: a request matching two
# rules inherits both, and a header set twice is joined with a comma rather
# than replaced, so the broader rule above has to be removed first.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
